WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.325
The six metrics.

2
00:00:01.325 --> 00:00:06.084
Two come from Module 6: the ninetieth
percentiles of separation-to-block,

3
00:00:06.084 --> 00:00:10.525
at most four hours, and
separation-to-revocation, at most twenty-four.

4
00:00:10.525 --> 00:00:13.998
Transfer-to-review comes from
Module 4's mover review,

5
00:00:13.998 --> 00:00:16.050
at most two hundred forty hours.

6
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:20.938
The joiner readiness rate comes from
Module 3, at least ninety-five percent.

7
00:00:20.938 --> 00:00:24.313
And two are computed by this
run: correlation coverage,

8
00:00:24.313 --> 00:00:29.113
the share of enabled accounts that
resolve to a current worker or contractor,

9
00:00:29.113 --> 00:00:32.338
at least ninety-nine percent;
and derivation purity,

10
00:00:32.338 --> 00:00:37.513
the share of access-granting memberships
computed by rule, at least eighty percent.

11
00:00:37.513 --> 00:00:43.325
Module 1's scan and Module 2's contractor
decisions feed the drift classes instead.

12
00:00:43.325 --> 00:00:48.850
One rule matters most here: a metric with
no input is not measured, never zero.

13
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.788
And the thresholds are the
program's starting values.

14
00:00:51.788 --> 00:00:55.660
Choosing them is the agency's
decision under C A seven.
